WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.277
A correlated scalar and a pre-aggregated join can sometimes produce the same result.

00:00:05.277 --> 00:00:08.277
The correlated form may be simpler to read.

00:00:08.277 --> 00:00:13.407
The derived-table form may be convenient when several aggregated features are needed.

00:00:13.407 --> 00:00:16.557
Do not assume one form is always faster.

00:00:16.557 --> 00:00:20.242
PostgreSQL can transform queries during optimization.

00:00:20.242 --> 00:00:25.182
Use correct semantics first, then inspect the plan on representative data.

00:00:25.182 --> 00:00:29.347
A correlated subquery refers to the current row of the outer query.

00:00:29.347 --> 00:00:34.422
Conceptually, the inner query is evaluated in relation to each outer row.

00:00:34.422 --> 00:00:39.602
That makes some business rules easy to express, but it can be expensive at scale.

00:00:39.602 --> 00:00:44.560
Compare a correlated formulation with a pre-aggregated join when performance matters.
